damnation:
We’re lost so! Shakspeare’s ghost could scarcely plead
Against our just damnation. Stand aside;
We’ll muse for comfort that, last century,

dam:
Lying fast asleep;
Like a river from its dam
Flashed the Tiger's leap.

dames:
"More than Latona's number will remain;
"Then hence, ye Theban dames, hence haste away,
"Nor longer off'rings to Latona pay;

damsel:
Beside her bed a whispered word:
'Damsel, rise up; be not afraid;
For I am come at last,' it said.

Folks jes' stan' stock-still a-sta'in', an' dey mos' nigh hol's dey bref;
An' de young mens, dey 's a-sayin', "I 's gwine mek dat damsel mine,"
When Angelina Johnson comes a-swingin' down de line.
